226	// an identifier across continuation. The chain never changes, so the failure
227	// is ErrInvalidArgument rather than ErrQueryChanged; even when the added
228	// identifier matches nothing and both filters hit the same transactions, the
229	// request still describes different conditions and yields no page. The
230	// original cursor and its statistics keep working afterwards.
